# REGRESSION GATE for issues/fixed/yo-test-does-not-forward-std-path-to-batch-compile.md.
#
# `--std-path` is a GLOBAL flag: main strips it from argv before subcommand
# dispatch and stashes it with the module manager. The RUNNER therefore honours
# it, but the child `yo compile` that builds the test batch is spawned with a
# fresh argv and used to fall back to YO_STD.
#
# So this case pins YO_STD to a path that does not exist while passing the REAL
# std via `--std-path`. Before the fix the runner evaluated fine and the child
# compile died looking for a prelude under /nonexistent; after it, both use the
# std the flag names. The harness normally exports YO_STD=$REPO_ROOT/std for
# every case, which is exactly what makes the override meaningful here.
#
# The golden keeps only the summary lines: batch compiles emit clang warnings
# whose text moves with the compiler version.
env=YO_STD=/nonexistent-std-so-only-std-path-can-work
stdout_keep=^(\$ yo |rc=|.*[0-9]+ passed|yo: error)
timeout=600
